I'm just throwing these out because I think they'd be cool for the monk 
class.

Monks should be able to [j]ump taking martial arts films into 
consideration. Of course it should be acquired at a decent level like 11.

Every monk's path of enlightenment and training is different. With each 
odd level, a monk has the potential to choose between two intrinsics. 
Say, for example, choosing between fire resistance and jumping at level 
11.

Of course there won't always be a choice and sometimes the RNG will 
choose one of the two at random for the monk in order to prevent people 
only playing one kind of monk with certain intrinsics.

The player must choose wisely, when given the option, because the skipped 
intrinsic won't be offered again.

Whenever I play my chaotic monk I always wish that he would be able to do 
a spinning roundhouse kick when surrounded by low-level (or any level) 
monsters. It'd be something like the mechanic in the NetHack banes patch 
for Giantslayer that on a critical hit when using [k]ick as an attack 1d8 
monsters will be hit in a row. Of course it'd be unavailable to armored 
monks despite the bug (feature?) that allows monks to successfully hit 
with kicks while wearing armor. Then again, who really uses [k]ick when 
attacking monsters? I only use it when I'm pudding dancing on DL 1-4.

Did I mention that being able to split boulders while wearing kicking 
boots w/ 18+ strength (the boots would prevent the toes from being hurt) 
or punching with gauntlets of power would be nice as well?

Also monks should take a greater hit on their piety (or perhaps luck) 
when consuming meat in the same way knights are more harshly punished for 
being unchivalrous in SPORKHack.

Pardon the pun but -1 to one's piety is not an impediment nor does it 
encourage the player to stick with the monk concept, it merely adds 
flavor if the monk follows the appropriate dietary conduct.

Here's a non-monk idea. Hitting a door with cockatrice eggs or throwing a 
cockatrice corpse against a door will turn the door into a wall. It'd be 
a nice defensive move since giants LOEV smashing doors and allow for some 
breathing room while healing up in crazy situations. Of course this would 
be no match for prepared dwarven attackers in hot pursuit, xorns, rock 
moles and other diggers of the earth. It wouldn't work on the door to a 
shop but it would piss off the shopkeeper.

Another non-monk idea. While poison-resistant and one gets the "You feel 
especially healthy!" then it should confer disease resistance. This would 
only apply to food poisoning and Pestilence not mummy rot (was re: bones 
files) nor lycanthropy. Why? I said so. Of course if this is still 
considered too unbalancing then the disease resistance should be a one-
shot much like the "You can recognize detrimental food" so the player 
gets a free pass but until the reaquire the disease resistance they're 
just as screwed as everyone else.

Finally this one is a bit more elaborate and it's based entirely on the 
prior YANIs. Monk players could be given the choice between playing a 
worldly monk, i.e. not celibate or vegetarian nor eschewing worldly 
goods, or an ascetic monk.

An ascetic monk would have conducts for celibacy just like in That Other 
Roguelike, a vow of poverty conduct (I don't know if it'd simply be 
avoiding gems, precious metals and expensive magical and non-magical 
items or if this would follow the example of the Vow of Poverty feat in 
Dungeons and Dragons see http://sarnath.heptapod.org/vow_of_poverty.jpg)

A worldly monk would be able to eat meat, losing only -1 piety without 
the guilty message, consort with foocubi while collecting various 
treasures. Yet certain things would be unavailable to the monk like 
choosing their intrinsics at odd levels. In short, just playing a normal 
3.4.3 monk without the You feel guilty message.


